    <GaugingStation location="Broadwey" name="Wey" number="44009">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V crump profile weir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Almost a full range station but bypassed along a road 1/2 mile u/s at highest flows. Structure capacity 3.3cumecs. Weedy river. First hand observation during 07/2012 event indicates the weir was still modular at 0.5m. Theoretical original rating. Upper limit of rating is 0.34m/1.02m3/s and flows are extrapolated beyond this limit. Flows affected by pumping at Friar Waddon. One peak flow rating across the period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V Crump profile weir, crest 4.5m wide, crest slopes 1:10.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">WY1991/1992 rejected as true AMAX likely occured during period of missing data. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural to within 10% at Q95. Sensibly natural regime, although substantial Gw abstraction affects headwaters at Upwey. Some hatch activity upstream but does not affect average daily flow.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly a limestone catchment, Kimmeridge Clay, Portland Sand, Purbeck beds. Land use is mainly pastoral agriculture. Runoff figures suggest topographical and hydrological catchment areas do not coincide. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">G</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED, confirming extrapolation of theoretical rating to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Limited validation of rating beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
